PDF root cause (confirmed, not a font/crop hypothesis)
  Supplied file: digital-small1, 332 physical PDF pages, 612 x 792 pt.
  Title metadata: digital-small1.
  Creator/Producer: calibre 2.26.0. Its input format is not recorded.
  All three fonts are embedded subsets of Times New Roman (regular/bold/italic).
  PDF is fixed-layout (pdf=true, reflow=false), not an EPUB being reflowed.
  Physical page 17: JENNIFER / Luve, Swaziland, Present Day.
  Physical page 19: EDWARD / Hampshire, England, Present Day.
  On p17 the large J's extracted bbox is [5,153.657,24.831,200.016].
  ENNIFER's bbox is [5,175.954,52.234,186.180]. They intersect in the source.
  On p19 E is [5,153.657,36.148,200.016]; DWARD is
  [5,175.954,46.105,186.180]. These also intersect before scaling.
  The source paints the initial before the page number, chapter heading and
  location. No indent is reserved. The source trace records the J as a
  68-unit glyph under a .75 scale (51 pt), at the same x=5 as body text.
  Independent mutool 1.28.6 at 200 DPI AND Poppler reproduce the collision.
  Device-resolution v0.4/v0.5 render-path PNGs are pixel-identical for both pages.
  Therefore neither font substitution, trim, screen transform, EPUB CSS nor
  reader reflow caused this visual error. The PDF's conversion layout is broken.
  EPUB origin is plausible from calibre metadata, but cannot be proved from it.
  Do not silently shift or squeeze text to fake a missing publisher layout.
  A correct original EPUB/PDF is needed for a source-faithful layout correction.
  The 21_* "after" PNGs intentionally show the still-broken source geometry.

Selection and annotations
  Strict word hit testing; whitespace is not treated as a remote nearest word.
  Bounded drag snapping. Visible slot page/generation gates hit testing.
  The exact stored render matrix maps crop offsets, scale and letterboxing.
  Long press uses the current stationary finger location. Drag selects complete
  words in forward/backward reading order on the current page only.
  Live DU feedback (black outlines visible in binary mode), REAGL on release.
  Two draggable handles; touch-to-word offsets prevent jumping when grabbed.
  Nearest-centre hit choice fixes overlapping hit regions on wrapped selections.
  Slot-0 Protocol B tracking prevents another finger changing selection.
  In extraction only, an isolated colliding initial is joined to its body word.
  This fixes selecting headings/location between the initial and body text.
  PDF drawing commands are not changed. PDF never receives user CSS.
  Tapping a mark opens Delete / Change style / Copy to notes / Cancel.
  Notes-list long press deletes. JSON and TXT are both rewritten after all edits.
  Legacy notes without timestamps work. Same-line quads are consolidated to
  avoid doubled underline baselines.

